    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d164">

                <pb facs="0369" n="295" sameAs="frus:frus1941-43/pg295"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Pacific War/1508: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Wellington </hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Cox</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">strictly confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wellington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-12-31T12:00:00+12:00">December 31,
                            1941—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]<anchor n="1" xml:id="d164-f1"/></seg>
                </opener>
                <p>Prime Minister Fraser has just told me that the position of New Zealand in the
                    Pacific war is a source of great anxiety. He has already communicated with Prime
                    Minister Churchill on the matter and assumes that his representations<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d164-f2"/> have been laid before the President. He continued
                    that he would appreciate any reports from me which would aid the United States
                    in understanding this country’s position. It was possible the Japanese would
                    by-pass New Zealand, but on the other hand he felt that if they succeeded in
                    progressing south an attack on New Zealand could be considered as probable. He
                    reasoned that it would be a feather in the Japanese cap to seize a part of the
                    British Empire which was peopled with the white race and whose defense was
                    slight. The Dominion would also provide a jumping off place for an attack on
                    Australia.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cox</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d164-f1" n="1" xml:id="d164-f1-content">
                <p>The omitted portion deals with specific military measures being taken by the
                    Government of New Zealand.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d164-f2" n="2" xml:id="d164-f2-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Supra.</hi>
                </p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
